  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Single-DGX-Spark Qwen3.8-27B on Ash Hart's TensorFold engine v0.4.0 (exact decoding, custom CUDA kernels JIT-compiled on first start, stock upstream source) with NVIDIA's ModelOpt NVFP4 export (NVFP4 MLP and language-model head, FP8 attention and DeltaNet projections, bf16 embeddings and gates) read as it ships, and z-lab's DFlash2 draft model, which TensorFold's CUDA engine requires unless drafting is switched off. One rank only: TensorFold's two-rank mode is not available here. Serves one request at a time by default (upstream CUDA default; the concurrency setting enables shared rounds) at the model's 262,144-token window. Text only: upstream stops at startup on --vision for this checkpoint until image input is qualified on it. Upstream measured 47 tok/s code and 38 tok/s chat on one DGX Spark (below its MLX 4-bit checkpoint's 58 and 50 on the same box) and a 62.5 GiB startup estimate at the 262,144-token window (upstream claims, unmeasured here). Licences, for information: Qwen3.8-27B and NVIDIA's NVFP4 export are Apache-2.0; z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 states Apache-2.0 on its model card (a mirror of incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2); TensorFold is MIT.",
    "tags": [
      "dflash2",
      "engine",
      "kernel-jit",
      "modelopt",
      "nvfp4",
      "qwen3.8",
      "reasoning",
      "spark",
      "speculative-decoding",
      "tensorfold"
    ],
    "title": "Qwen3.8 27B NVFP4 TensorFold single Spark"
  },
